WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.033
Lab 2 does it for real, in a test
domain with one domain controller,

2
00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:08.188
never production, as a Domain Admin,
with a member server for the host.

3
00:00:08.188 --> 00:00:11.624
Nobody has run it yet, so no
step's output has been seen.

4
00:00:11.624 --> 00:00:14.582
Steps one to four are the
setup: the K D S root key,

5
00:00:14.582 --> 00:00:20.029
backdated only in this single domain controller
test domain and only if none exists,

6
00:00:20.029 --> 00:00:24.387
the two O Us, the creators group with
its right, and the pipeline's G M S A.

7
00:00:24.387 --> 00:00:29.162
Step five creates the timesheet G M S
A by hand, the way the pipeline would.

8
00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.512
Step six, on the host after a restart,

9
00:00:31.512 --> 00:00:35.238
installs and tests it, and sets
a test service to run as it.

10
00:00:35.238 --> 00:00:38.406
Step seven backs out the
G M S A and its group,

11
00:00:38.406 --> 00:00:41.212
and keeps the setup, which is made once.

12
00:00:41.212 --> 00:00:44.218
In any domain with more
than one domain controller,

13
00:00:44.218 --> 00:00:46.940
use Effective Immediately
and wait ten hours.
